From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Local build <local@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:24:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FIX wayland backend: set the layer's image description only
 when its color changes

The layer compared its color description with the previous one as
shared_ptrs, by pointer: the compositor gives the primary layer a new
description object every frame (layerBlendingColor()->withHdrMetadata()),
so the nested KWin created and set a new image description on the host
every frame (seen in Hyprland's trace: a parametric creator, six setters,
create, set_image_description per frame, all with the same values).
---
 src/backends/wayland/wayland_layer.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_layer.cpp b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_layer.cpp
index 311be7f..87c1abe 100644
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_layer.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_layer.cpp
@@ -101,7 +101,9 @@ void WaylandLayer::commit(PresentationMode presentationMode)
         m_viewport->setDestination(logicalTarget.size());
     }
     m_subSurface->setPosition(logicalTarget.topLeft());
-    if (m_colorSurface && m_color != m_previousColor) {
+    // by value: the compositor gives the layer a new description object every frame (withHdrMetadata), and the
+    // shared_ptr comparison found here compares pointers - a new image description went to the host every frame
+    if (m_colorSurface && (!m_color || !m_previousColor || *m_color != *m_previousColor)) {
         const auto imageDescription = output->backend()->display()->colorManager()->createImageDescription(*m_color);
         wp_color_management_surface_v1_set_image_description(m_colorSurface, imageDescription, WP_COLOR_MANAGER_V1_RENDER_INTENT_PERCEPTUAL);
         wp_image_description_v1_destroy(imageDescription);
